From 32050946f0458ec0f2570e2815460155d0745ce0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:21:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: report O1 while waiting for GPON PHY sync

The OMCI device state is zero-initialized and was previously updated only
when the PLOAM state callback ran. Deferring MAC initialization until the
xPON PHY is synchronized can therefore expose state 0 to userspace while
the software PLOAM state is correctly waiting in O1.

Initialize the OMCI-visible state to O1 immediately after registering the
backend. Later PLOAM state transitions continue to update it normally.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index b9ce2fdc297d..b270a2e4b8a4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -2564,6 +2564,12 @@ static int gpon_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_put_gdm;
 
+	/*
+	 * The OMCI device is zero-initialized. Publish O1 before the
+	 * deferred PHY synchronization path can leave the MAC uninitialized.
+	 */
+	airoha_gpon_omci_set_state(&priv->omci, GPON_O1_INITIAL);
+
 	priv->omci_handler.rx = airoha_gpon_omci_receive;
 	priv->omci_handler.priv = &priv->omci;
 	ret = airoha_eth_register_xpon_oam(priv->gdm_dev,
